Problem: E-Commerce Restock Notification System

Core Goal: Automatically notify interested customers when an out-of-stock product becomes available again.

Requirements:
    Product State:
     A product tracks its stockCount (starts at 0) and a list of interested users.
    User Actions: Customers can subscribe to or unsubscribe from alerts for a specific product.
    Restock Trigger: Adding inventory (addStock(int quantity)) transitions the product from out-of-stock (0) to in-stock (greater than 0).

Notification Channels:
    Email Alert: Sends an email notification to subscribed users.
    SMS Alert: Sends a text message to subscribed users.
    App Push Alert: Sends a mobile push notification to subscribed users.
    Constraint: Notifications should only fire when stock changes from 0 to greater than 0 (not when adding more stock to an already available item), and new notification channels must be pluggable without changing the product class.